# Tide Line

Free Gotham Whale app. Kids (7–14) follow New York humpback whales. Adults use Observer mode. One phase at a time; do not start the next phase until the user replies "continue."

## Children's privacy (COPPA)

- Children never create accounts or enter email. A verified parent or teacher owns each child profile.
- Child profiles store only a picker nickname (no free text), avatar, age band, and progress. No real names, photos of kids, or contact info.
- No chat, comments, or free-text input from children.
- No ads. No third-party analytics, crash reporters, or SDKs that collect device IDs or advertising IDs.
- Never store a child's precise location. Location checks stay on-device; save only quest id + date.

```ts
// BAD — child's coordinates must never be stored or sent
await supabase.from("quest_completions").insert({ child_id, lat, lng });

// GOOD
await supabase.from("quest_completions").insert({ child_id, quest_id, completed_on });
```

- Every table has Row Level Security. Adults access only their own children. Teachers access only their own classes.
- Kids' notifications go through the parent or teacher device, worded for kids.

## Adults (Observer mode)

- Precise location and photo metadata only after explicit consent.
- Public map locations are rounded to 2 decimal places.

## Wildlife safety

- Never award points for proximity to animals.
- Copy must say to stay at least 100 yards from whales and to go to the water with a grown-up.

## Environment and security

- GitHub, Vercel, and Supabase. Two Supabase projects: DEV and PRODUCTION.
- Migrations run against DEV only unless the user explicitly types "production."
- Every schema change is a file in `supabase/migrations/`.
- Never hardcode keys. Read environment variables. `.env*` is gitignored. `.env.example` has placeholder names only.
- Never use the Supabase service role key in client code. The app uses only the public anon key.
- Expo EAS builds the mobile app. Vercel hosts only web routes (teacher dashboard, science review, public map, donation pages).

## Style

- Warm, curious language at about a grade 3 reading level.
- Minimum 48px tap targets, high contrast, dynamic text size, and respect "reduce motion."
- Works offline where reasonable (cached tales, cached whale cards, queued submissions).

## Tech stack

- Expo (React Native) + TypeScript strict + Expo Router
- Supabase: Postgres, Auth, Storage, Row Level Security, PostGIS
- Zustand for local state
- react-native-reanimated, lottie-react-native, rive-react-native, expo-haptics, expo-av, expo-speech, expo-location, expo-notifications, expo-image-picker
- Jest + React Native Testing Library; pgTAP for database tests
- Vercel for web routes; EAS for mobile builds

Before adding a package, say what it is, why it is needed, and confirm it does not collect device identifiers or send data to third parties.
